WEBVTT

00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:04.424
A connected service moment begins with uncertainty. Asset 360

00:00:04.424 --> 00:00:08.310
brings authorized appliance evidence into the flow of work, so

00:00:08.310 --> 00:00:12.322
teams can move from a reported issue to the next useful question

00:00:12.322 --> 00:00:14.328
without guessing at a diagnosis.

00:00:15.600 --> 00:00:19.894
In Dynamics 365 Customer Service, the case remains the workspace.

00:00:19.894 --> 00:00:24.121
Asset 360 opens beside the existing Service Toolkit and resolves

00:00:24.121 --> 00:00:28.151
the saved case to its assigned appliance. Profile information

00:00:28.151 --> 00:00:31.784
stays separate from connected evidence, and the service

00:00:31.784 --> 00:00:36.012
representative never has to leave the case to understand what is

00:00:36.012 --> 00:00:36.408
known.

00:00:41.600 --> 00:00:45.814
For a Cove dishwasher reported as not draining, the view separates

00:00:45.814 --> 00:00:50.029
observations from interpretation. The example shows repeated drain

00:00:50.029 --> 00:00:54.180
attempts, no reported level change, source time, and missing-data

00:00:54.180 --> 00:00:58.203
behavior. Those signals support focused validation, but they do

00:00:58.203 --> 00:01:01.906
not prove a root cause, prescribe a repair, or declare the

00:01:01.906 --> 00:01:02.864
appliance safe.

00:01:07.600 --> 00:01:11.617
The Connected Appliance Advisor publishes the same protected,

00:01:11.617 --> 00:01:15.633
read-only service contract into Microsoft 365 Copilot. A case

00:01:15.633 --> 00:01:19.979
number resolves to the authorized appliance through a bounded tool

00:01:19.979 --> 00:01:23.799
call. The response labels synthetic data, returns only the

00:01:23.799 --> 00:01:27.947
requested context, and stops instead of silently taking another

00:01:27.947 --> 00:01:28.408
action.

00:01:32.600 --> 00:01:36.576
In Copilot Cowork, the installed Asset 360 plugin uses that

00:01:36.576 --> 00:01:40.890
protected service directly. One profile-mode snapshot mounts the

00:01:40.890 --> 00:01:45.203
native Microsoft MCP Apps renderer and the interactive appliance

00:01:45.203 --> 00:01:49.584
card. History and explanation tools remain untouched, and no case

00:01:49.584 --> 00:01:54.032
update, message, appliance command, or repair action is performed.

00:01:58.600 --> 00:02:02.680
Across each surface, identity and permissions stay behind the

00:02:02.680 --> 00:02:07.094
experience. The system presents evidence, freshness, unknowns, and

00:02:07.094 --> 00:02:11.441
a next validation question. Qualified people still decide whether

00:02:11.441 --> 00:02:15.588
to continue troubleshooting, contact Customer Care, or arrange

00:02:15.588 --> 00:02:16.792
certified service.

00:02:18.600 --> 00:02:22.440
One governed evidence contract, available where service work

00:02:22.440 --> 00:02:26.472
happens. The next step is to validate an approved customer data

00:02:26.472 --> 00:02:29.544
sample and measure the service outcome together.
